oto/134787193.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bryan Cranston transformed a quaint beach bungalow into a stunning net-zero energy residence in Venice, California. The redesigned home showcases sleek modern aesthetics paired with cutting-edge sustainable energy solutions, reflecting eco-conscious principles. Listed in 2021, it achieved an impressive sale of $5.45 million, exceeding its initial purchase price. This remarkable project exemplifies the potential of sustainable living within today’s competitive real estate landscape.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2007-bryan-cranston-bought-a-california-beach-bungalow-for-2-5-million-after-rebuilding-it-as-a-2450-sq-ft-net-zero-energy-home-he-sold-the-property-14-years-later-for-5-45-million/articleshow/134787193.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2007-bryan-cranston-bought-a-california-beach-bungalow-for-2-5-million-after-rebuilding-it-as-a-2450-sq-ft-net-zero-energy-home-he-sold-the-property-14-years-later-for-5-45-million/articleshow/134787193.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134787355,imgsize-125389.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New extinct crocodile found in Sphinx rocks, with a missing snout tip]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134774380.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/scientists-identified-a-new-extinct-crocodile-species-from-the-same-egyptian-rocks-used-to-build-the-great-sphinx-even-the-fossil-is-missing-the-tip-of-its-snout-echoing-the-monument/articleshow/134774380.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/scientists-identified-a-new-extinct-crocodile-species-from-the-same-egyptian-rocks-used-to-build-the-great-sphinx-even-the-fossil-is-missing-the-tip-of-its-snout-echoing-the-monument/articleshow/134774380.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T03:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134774396,imgsize-425866.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Doe swatted amid threats: Police respond to fake shooting call; FBI investigates case]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134797082.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cornell-jane-doe-faces-death-threats-doxxing-after-armed-cops-swarm-family-home/articleshow/134797082.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/cornell-jane-doe-faces-death-threats-doxxing-after-armed-cops-swarm-family-home/articleshow/134797082.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T23:12:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134797326,imgsize-77028.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Zach Bryan’s New Retreat: singer buys $18.25 million Leiper’s Fork estate; adds on-site studio]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134779303.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Earlier this year, Zach Bryan made headlines by purchasing a sprawling estate in Leiper's Fork, Tennessee, valued at $18.25 million. This stunning property boasts nearly 40 acres of breathtaking views and luxury amenities, including a professional recording studio tailored for his music career. It showcases Bryan's desire for privacy, while still being conveniently located near the vibrant Nashville music scene.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/country-singer-zach-bryan-quietly-bought-an-18-million-tennessee-estate-in-2026-the-secluded-property-sits-on-146-acres-and-includes-a-6000-square-foot-main-house-and-recording-studio/articleshow/134779303.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/country-singer-zach-bryan-quietly-bought-an-18-million-tennessee-estate-in-2026-the-secluded-property-sits-on-146-acres-and-includes-a-6000-square-foot-main-house-and-recording-studio/articleshow/134779303.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T02:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134779309,imgsize-475270.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Floyd V. Bowlin-Lemon: Arkansas court upholds fence boundary; $12,000 treble damages stand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134764147.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent ruling upheld the Bowlin family's claim regarding a fence that served as a property boundary since 1967. This decision followed a dispute over the removal of the fence and trees by neighboring property owners. The Arkansas Court of Appeals affirmed damages of $12,000 due to intentional tree removal and ordered the reconstruction of the fence.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arkansas-family-treated-the-same-fence-as-its-property-line-for-nearly-six-decades-after-new-neighbours-removed-fencing-and-trees-an-appeals-court-upheld-12000-in-treble-damages-and-an-order-to-rebuild-the-fence/articleshow/134764147.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-arkansas-family-treated-the-same-fence-as-its-property-line-for-nearly-six-decades-after-new-neighbours-removed-fencing-and-trees-an-appeals-court-upheld-12000-in-treble-damages-and-an-order-to-rebuild-the-fence/articleshow/134764147.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134764210,imgsize-1587925.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Federal executive created fake program, diverted $145M; FBI found 298 gold bars in $193.6M fraud]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134791260.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a shocking turn of events, David J. Rush, a former high-ranking federal employee, has admitted guilt in a case of extensive fraud against the US government. Using his top-secret clearance, he concocted imaginary government projects to pocket nearly $194 million. His lavish spending spree included luxury objects and assets, leading to an FBI raid that uncovered gold bars and cash.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/federal-executive-with-top-secret-clearance-created-a-fake-classified-program-and-diverted-145-million-into-luxury-property-and-gold-after-fbi-found-298-gold-bars-he-pleaded-guilty-to-a-193-6-million-fraud/articleshow/134791260.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/federal-executive-with-top-secret-clearance-created-a-fake-classified-program-and-diverted-145-million-into-luxury-property-and-gold-after-fbi-found-298-gold-bars-he-pleaded-guilty-to-a-193-6-million-fraud/articleshow/134791260.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T00:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134791359,imgsize-2315989.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida Land Acquisition: Disney secretly bought 27,443 acres; deal reshaped Walt Disney World]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134760710.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Walt Disney initiated a secret land acquisition strategy in Florida to develop Walt Disney World. The effort involved purchasing over 27,000 acres through front companies to maintain anonymity. This acquisition began in 1964 and was publicly revealed in 1965. While Disney did not survive to see the completion, his vision ultimately changed entertainment in America. The project included creating the Reedy Creek Improvement District for efficient management of infrastructure.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/walt-disney-quietly-assembled-more-than-27000-acres-in-florida-through-secret-transactions-for-about-5-million-averaging-roughly-182-an-acre-after-the-buyers-identity-emerged-the-land-became-walt-disney-world/articleshow/134760710.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/walt-disney-quietly-assembled-more-than-27000-acres-in-florida-through-secret-transactions-for-about-5-million-averaging-roughly-182-an-acre-after-the-buyers-identity-emerged-the-land-became-walt-disney-world/articleshow/134760710.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134760744,imgsize-1047091.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oxford study suggests animals may have evolved 200 million years earlier]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134788319.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/a-new-oxford-led-study-suggests-animal-life-may-have-begun-700-to-800-million-years-ago-up-to-200-million-years-earlier-than-the-clearest-fossil-record-and-possibly-before-snowball-earth/articleshow/134788319.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/a-new-oxford-led-study-suggests-animal-life-may-have-begun-700-to-800-million-years-ago-up-to-200-million-years-earlier-than-the-clearest-fossil-record-and-possibly-before-snowball-earth/articleshow/134788319.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T23:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134788372,imgsize-487068.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US bill proposes raising H-1B violation fines to $250,000 and 10-year ban]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134796921.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A proposed bill aims to raise penalties against employers violating H-1B visa rules significantly. Introduced by Beth Van Duyne, the legislation is under consideration in the House. Proposed fines would increase from thousands to hundreds of thousands of dollars for serious violations. In addition, the legislation would extend bans on employers from three years to ten years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-house-bill-proposes-raising-serious-h-1b-violation-fines-from-35000-to-250000-and-extending-employer-bans-from-at-least-3-years-to-10-years-as-washingtons-visa-crackdown-intensifies/articleshow/134796921.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-house-bill-proposes-raising-serious-h-1b-violation-fines-from-35000-to-250000-and-extending-employer-bans-from-at-least-3-years-to-10-years-as-washingtons-visa-crackdown-intensifies/articleshow/134796921.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T23:01:33+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://pur